turbo-heresy is a parody reskin of turbo-bible. It ships none of the
eleven Bible translations the original bundles; instead it embeds the
three public-domain / original "scriptures" below, each under its own
terms:

──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
Bundled scriptures:

  en-plost      Paradise Lost — John Milton (1667)            Public Domain
  en-liber-al   Liber AL vel Legis — Aleister Crowley (1904)  Public Domain*
  en-unholy     The Unholy Writ — original parody             CC0-1.0

  * Liber AL vel Legis is public domain in jurisdictions applying a
    life-plus-70-years term (Crowley died 1947) — in effect since 2018.
    Ordo Templi Orientis contests its U.S. copyright status. Bundled
    here for personal, non-commercial use.

Paradise Lost is sourced from Project Gutenberg eBook #26 (public
domain). Liber AL vel Legis is transcribed from a widely-circulated
public-domain edition. The Unholy Writ is an original CC0-1.0 work.

The texts are built into per-translation SQLite databases by
data/heresy/build_heresy.py; turbo-heresy does not alter their wording
beyond whitespace normalization.

──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
turbo-heresy is an independent parody and is not affiliated with,
